# Tips To Win

1. First ultimate thing is your video. It should be clear and easy to follow. Show your thinking and pitch yourself.
2. Spend your first few hours on the brand, not on Figma. Decide your colour, type, voice and button style before you place a single section.
3. Write your copy in a plain document first. If it does not convince in black text on a white page, no gradient is going to save it.
4. Solve the refund explanation before anything else. It is the hardest part of this brief and the biggest reason people drop off.
5. Say one thing per section. A section trying to say three things is saying nothing.
6. Buttons are copy too. Name them the way a person would say it.
7. Test it on a friend or a parent. Ask them what we sell and how the refund works. Their answer is your score.
8. Less is better. If you are unsure about a section, cut it.
9. **Take mobile seriously. Do not leave it as three rushed frames at the end.**
10. Think about the edge cases and mention them in your file. What does the page show to someone who has already bought a course. What happens when a course is sold out or a batch is closed. How do you show the price when there is a discount, a combo and a refund all sitting on the same card.

